# DS Interactive Handbook Changelog
*Last Updated: March 6, 2026*

## v1.6.5
- Worldmap: Added 4 new biome encounter libraries (Ossuite Tribal Lands, Perilous Ossuite Tribal Lands, Darkling Tribal Conflict Zones, Darkling Infantry HQ).
- Worldmap: Conflict-zone presets include an "already fighting" note (uses preset encounters so the note is visible).
- Data: Biome encounter tables validated against the V2 bestiary.

## Major Game Updates & New Features

### Diapered Defenders: VR Module — Handbook-Themed Overhaul (New)
- Visuals/Theme:
  - Full handbook style applied (parchment browns, warm gold accents, MedievalSharp/Cormorant typography), gold-lined panels, and textured parchment backgrounds.
  - Themed hover cards for monsters/objects with rollable actions (when runtime bestiary is available) and concise traits preview otherwise.
- Board/UX:
  - No scroll containers. The board now fits the available width first and only shrinks for height overflow; keyboard zoom (+/−/0) supported.
  - Hard-coded player spawns per room are always used on entry; drag/drop is purely visual and does not persist positions across rooms.
  - Next button starts disabled each room and only enables when all room requirements are satisfied.
- Gameplay/Logic:
  - Room completion now requires all monsters defeated and any room puzzle requirements met. Crystal switches (e.g., Scriptorium) must be deactivated before proceeding.
  - Scriptorium fix: You can no longer leave immediately; deactivating the sustaining crystal and clearing the room is required.
  - Malodorous Balance: Debris layering adjusted so player tokens can stand on the central debris as intended.
  - Trap interactions surfaced in the log (e.g., gas vents) when stepped on or triggered.
- Data & Integrations:
  - Supports runtime bestiary (full stat cards) with graceful fallback to built-in monster previews.
  - Puzzle system supports both room-level and layout-level definitions (dais/object placements), with immediate validation and reset on failure.

### Old War Defense - Complete Overhaul
- **Cleric Tower Added:** New support tower with 6 unique cleric tokens and a champion ("The Holy Protector"). Buffs nearby towers, can cleanse debuffs, and grants immunity to curse/disable.
- **Game Modes:**
  - **Hard Mode:** Shorter, straighter path, 600 starting essence, more intense gameplay.
  - **Chaos/Horde Mode:** Endless waves of titans, titan beasts, hordes, diggers, fliers, and non-path enemies. Start with 10,000 essence.
- **Portal System Overhaul:**
  - Portals spawn from early waves, with more locations and frequency as the game progresses.
  - All non-boss, non-digger enemies can exit portals at high levels.
- **Enemy Variety:**
  - All 101 monster sprites implemented and used in spawn patterns.
  - Titan beasts and abominations now move straight, are larger, and have theatrical movement.
  - Improved spawn spacing for large enemies and hordes to prevent clustering.
- **UI/UX Improvements:**
  - Essence, lives, and wave counters moved below the game board, styled for clarity.
  - Mode buttons (Hard/Chaos) moved below the map for better access.
  - Wave details and notifications now appear in a fixed box under the board.
  - Tower purchase buttons shrunk to fit more options.
  - Tower token borders replaced with glowing underlays for a sharper look.
  - PNG scaling improved for crisp visuals.
- **Cheat Console:**
  - Activate with ` and =, enter codes for instant essence, upgrades, or wave skips.

